<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $104.1 mln Sept 17.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $104.1 mln Sept 17.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $104.1 million surplus on Sept. 17 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON SEPTEMBER 17</p>
<p>Exports: $206 million</p>
<p>Imports: $218.3 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $214.3 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $97.9 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $104.1 million</p>
<p>SEPTEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.579 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.925 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.714 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.304 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $64 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
</text>
